# AI Layer Maintenance

- Keep rules short, scoped, and actionable. Prefer several focused files over one long handbook.
- Skills should teach a reusable workflow, not duplicate repository prose.
- Commands are legacy-compatible convenience prompts. Keep them task-shaped and concise.
- Hooks must have a clear operational purpose: safety, context economy, or predictable execution.
- When the repo changes materially, update the relevant docs and AI-layer artifacts in the same change.
